@page "/components/input-otp"

<PageTitle>Input OTP — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Input OTP</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    Six real inputs, not one hidden field with painted boxes. It posts without JavaScript,
    <code>autocomplete="one-time-code"</code> on the first box lets a phone offer the code it has
    just received, and nothing needs rehydrating after a fragment swap.
</p>
<p class="doc-note">
    The compiler adds only what typing expects: advance on entry, retreat <i>and</i> clear on
    backspace, and a paste of the whole code filling every box. The server sees one value, because
    a hidden input is kept in step — six named fields would push the joining into every handler.
</p>

